==Battleground==
*1 [[Big Sal]] spawns as the boss after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Camelle]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 60% HP:
**1 [[Camelle]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 40% HP:
**1 [[Camelle]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 20% HP:
**1 [[Camelle]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage can be cheesed easily with the right cats (e.g. [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Freshman Cat Jobs]], [[Mighty Bomburr (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Bomburr]], or [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer]]), even in 3 crowns, but it is very hard otherwise, as you don't just need to deal with Sal but also with 4 Camelles. [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] is very useful for the Camelle part, as it can keep him perfectly stalled just in time for the next one, even in 3 crown. Otherwise, one or two decent health meatshields or [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]] can stall each Camelle just fine. Use tanky damage dealers like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|his manic variant]] to chip each Camelle slowly and finish the stage. For the part with Big Sal, there are many possible strategies:

*Using anti-Zombie Crowd controllers to prevent Big Sal from being able to hit the base. Just make sure that they do not damage the enemy base enough to bring out a Camelle.
*Using [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Professor Cat Jobs]], you can weaken Big Sal to the point that he does only 2400 damage to the base, giving you plenty of time to kill him. [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]] should be used to prevent Big Sal reviving and Cat Jobs walking past him. Do note that even with the Antimatter Fruit treasure maxed out, Cat Jobs will not be able to permaweaken Big Sal, meaning that there is a tiny window of opportunity for him to one hit your base. This can be prevented by bringing along a Weaken Effect Up (M) combo and a Weaken Effect Up (Sm).
*Using [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Kubilan Pasalan]], [[Piledriver Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Piledriver Cat]], or Mighty Bomburr, you can constantly knock the boss back, especially with the help of KB up combos, so all you have to do is wait for Sal to be super close to the base, summon your chosen unit and watch as they keep the boss away from the base. You may also want to accompany these with Backliner Zombie Killers such as [[Mighty Rekon Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Rekon Korps]] to speed up the process.
**For Bomburr, spawn him alone and watch as he makes Big Sal unable to do anything. His attack rate and Big Sal's slow movement speed allows it to keep him in a constant [[Knockback]] loop until he eventually dies, and he will dispatch Big Sal quickly enough.
**With Piledriver, add [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cats]] (don't use her true form due to increased speed) and maybe add some Zombie Killer Ubers with slow speed and long range, so they don't get too close.
**With Kubilan, you have to use Ubers such as Mighty Rekon Korps or [[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Drednot]] to take down the boss, due to Kubilan's long time between attacks.
*Using [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer]] and Combos, perma-[[Freeze|freeze]] the boss at the base and kill it with multiple [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cats]] or other powerful Zombie Killer cats.
*It is worth noting that [[Meditation Cat (Special Cat)]] can permastall Big Sal in front of the Cat Base with 200% Antimatter fruit treasures from Cats of the Cosmos.

After killing Sal, lure out a Camelle, lure him closer to your base to kill him, and repeat for each. Killing Camelle can be done with [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tankers]] like Jamiera Cat/Manic Jamiera Cat or tanky and damaging spammable units, like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] or [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]].


An alternate strategy for dealing with the Camelles is to use [[Haniwa Cat]], one other meatshield, [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Great]], and any other long-distance units that outrange Camelle to stall the Camelles at the base as your long distance units slowly wittle the base down.

